content.text:
Add updateGarageFraming near initShowroom / enterMenu.

We need to account for actual stage region. Let's define:

```
function updateGarageFraming() {
  if (!showroom) return;
  if (appState !== 'garage') { showroom.setViewShift(0); return; }
  const stage = dom.garageOrbit?.parentElement;
  if (!stage) return;
  const rect = stage.getBoundingClientRect();
  if (!rect.height) return;
  const h = window.innerHeight || 1;
  const center = rect.top + rect.height / 2;
  const shift = clamp(h / 2 - center, -h * 0.28, h * 0.28);
  showroom.setViewShift(shift);
}
```

But wait: the stage starts below header. Should we use rect.top + rect.height*0.5? The car extends vertically; maybe center slightly lower +5%. Use 0.5.

Also, on desktop, `garage-stage-copy` at top-left might overlap. Car is center; okay.

Call after setScreen. Also reset when menu.

`showroom.setMode('garage')` might change fov in update next frame which calls updateProjectionMatrix — but view offset remains. fine.

Add in enterGarage:
```
showroom?.setViewShift(0); // before layout? no
requestAnimationFrame(updateGarageFraming);
setTimeout(updateGarageFraming, 60); // ensure after screen transition/layout
```
The screen visibility transition only opacity, layout already full. But stage/dock need layout; synchronous getBoundingClientRect after class change forces layout. So immediate call works. Still rAF for safety.

enterMenu: showroom?.setViewShift(0).

onResize: after aspect updates, call updateGarageFraming() (guarded).

Also ResizeObserver on stage/dock to update when dock content size changes (e.g. part tabs wrap). Add in boot/wireEvents.

Let me insert function after initShowroom.

