Now wire events for orbit. Insert in wireEvents near btnGarage. Also double click reset, keyboard.

Need to think about pointer capture and `lostpointercapture`. Use setPointerCapture.

Also dragging on touch should prevent scroll. touch-action:none handles.

Add haptic? no.

Implement:
```
  const orbit = dom.garageOrbit;
  if (orbit) {
    let activePointer = null, lastX = 0, lastT = 0;
    const markUsed = () => dom.garageOrbitHint?.classList.add('is-used');
    orbit.addEventListener('pointerdown', (e) => {
      if (appState !== 'garage') return;
      if (e.pointerType === 'mouse' && e.button !== 0) return;
      activePointer = e.pointerId;
      lastX = e.clientX;
      lastT = performance.now();
      orbit.setPointerCapture?.(e.pointerId);
      showroom?.beginOrbit();
      markUsed();
      e.preventDefault();
    });
    orbit.addEventListener('pointermove', (e) => {
      if (activePointer !== e.pointerId) return;
      const now = performance.now();
      const dt = Math.max(0.008, (now - lastT) / 1000);
      const dx = e.clientX - lastX;
      lastX = e.clientX;
      lastT = now;
      showroom?.orbitBy(dx, dt);
    });
    const stop = (e) => {
      if (e.pointerId !== activePointer) return;
      activePointer = null;
      showroom?.endOrbit();
      try { orbit.releasePointerCapture?.(e.pointerId); } catch {}
    };
    orbit.addEventListener('pointerup', stop);
    orbit.addEventListener('pointercancel', stop);
    orbit.addEventListener('lostpointercapture', (e) => {
      if (activePointer === e.pointerId) { activePointer=null; showroom?.endOrbit(); }
    });
    orbit.addEventListener('dblclick', () => {
      showroom?.resetOrbit();
      dom.garageOrbitHint?.classList.remove('is-used');
      audio.click(520);
    });
    orbit.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
      let handled = true;
      if (e.key === 'ArrowLeft') showroom?.nudgeOrbit(e.shiftKey ? 0.45 : 0.18);
      else if (e.key === 'ArrowRight') showroom?.nudgeOrbit(e.shiftKey ? -0.45 : -0.18);
      else if (e.key === 'Home' || e.key.toLowerCase() === 'r') {
        showroom?.resetOrbit();
        dom.garageOrbitHint?.classList.remove('is-used');
      } else handled = false;
      if (handled) {
        e.preventDefault();
        markUsed();
        audio.click(420);
      }
    });
    // Reset the hint when entering the garage.
  }
```
Wait: nudge left should rotate car left. manualAngle += for ArrowLeft; sign visual unknown. Fine.

The hint "is-used" hides after first interaction. On re-enter garage, should it show again? If user already knows, keep hidden. But if reset on double click, show again maybe. That's what we do. However if manualAngle persists, hint hidden. Fine.

Need `audio` is imported object. yes.

ResizeObserver:
```
if (window.ResizeObserver) {
  const observer = new ResizeObserver(() => updateGarageFraming());
  if (dom.garageOrbit?.parentElement) observer.observe(dom.garageOrbit.parentElement);
  const dock = dom.garage?.querySelector('.garage-dock');
  if (dock) observer.observe(dock);
}
```
Potential feedback: updateGarageFraming sets camera only, no DOM. fine.

But warning: ResizeObserver callback may fire while appState garage; good.

Also `document.fonts.ready.then(updateGarageFraming)` maybe after boot to ensure layout labels? Not needed.

onResize: add `updateGarageFraming();` after camera updates. But onResize is called at boot before showroom? It runs after initShowroom in boot (boot calls initShowroom then enterMenu then onResize). showroom exists, appState menu → sets 0. fine.

Add onResize edit later.

